From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=B6rg=20Thalheim?= <joerg@thalheim.io>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:35:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kpropd: listen on a loopback-only host
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

get_wildcard_addr() passes AI_ADDRCONFIG, which makes getaddrinfo()
ignore loopback addresses when deciding whether IPv4 or IPv6 is
configured. On a host whose only interface is lo (containers, build
sandboxes running the test suite) both lookups fail with EAI_NONAME, the
do_standalone() child exits, and in iprop mode the parent keeps
requesting full resyncs that can never be delivered: t_iprop.py hangs.

Retry without AI_ADDRCONFIG before giving up.

Signed-off-by: Jörg Thalheim <joerg@thalheim.io>
---
 src/kprop/kpropd.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kprop/kpropd.c b/src/kprop/kpropd.c
index 4b36752..2762132 100644
--- a/src/kprop/kpropd.c
+++ b/src/kprop/kpropd.c
@@ -373,6 +373,13 @@ get_wildcard_addr(struct addrinfo **res)
     if (error == 0)
         return 0;
     hints.ai_family = AF_INET;
+    error = getaddrinfo(NULL, port, &hints, res);
+    if (error == 0)
+        return 0;
+    /* AI_ADDRCONFIG disregards loopback addresses: a host with no other
+     * interface configured (a container or build sandbox) has none left. */
+    hints.ai_flags = AI_PASSIVE;
+    hints.ai_family = AF_UNSPEC;
     return getaddrinfo(NULL, port, &hints, res);
 }
 
